## Round TW1b: a person's Twitch access (Options → Data and privacy).

# Options → Data and privacy's row: Twitch access a room's features use (about 16
# letters).
twitch-access = Twitch access
# The row's note when nothing is connected, or the person is signed out.
twitch-none = Nothing connected
# The row's description then: what it is for, one quiet line.
twitch-about = A room's host connects it from Host options to keep out the people they banned or blocked on Twitch or to show their chat; a player connects it to see a host's chat (Options → Multiplayer → Twitch chat in rooms).
# The row's note when connected.
# Variables:
#   $login (String) - the Twitch account
#   $features (String) - what it reads, listed (the feature words below)
twitch-connected = { $login }: { $features }
# What each connected feature is, in a list (lowercase where the language
# has case).
twitch-feature-bans = bans and timeouts
twitch-feature-blocks = blocks
twitch-feature-chat = chat
# The row's button, and the confirmation's (about 12 letters).
twitch-disconnect = Disconnect
# The row's description while connected.
twitch-connected-description = Kept on my server, never in the game; deleted after 30 days unused and when you sign out.
# The confirmation's title and text.
twitch-confirm = Disconnect Twitch access?
twitch-confirm-body = It is deleted from my server and revoked at Twitch. If your room keeps out your Twitch bans or shows your chat, that turns off at once there, and nobody is removed.
# The notice after.
twitch-notice-disconnected = Twitch access disconnected.
